{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBeta"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_one_sub_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_one_sub_pow","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L216-L233","doc":"**The per-row hook identity, q-analogue.**\n\n`∏_{j<a} (1 − Q^{h(j)}) · ∏ (β-gaps as `1 − Q^{gap}`) = ∏_{k=1}^{a+|t|} (1 − Q^k)`,\n\nwhere `h(j) = (a − j) + cnt t j` runs over the hook lengths of the row.  This is\n`rowHookProdF_mul_betaGapProdF` at `f n = 1 − Qⁿ`; it needs no separate proof because the original\nargument never touched the values, only the exponents.\n\nThis is the per-row half of the hook-length input that\n`QOU.Mathlib.LagrangeCoeffSum.sum_eq_bracket_mul_of_qratio_scaling` is waiting on.  What remains is\nto assemble the rows (`SYTHookFormulaBetaProd.prodHooks_eq_prod_rowHookProd`, likewise arithmetic-free\nin shape) and to recognise the assembled β-gap product as the Vandermonde denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_id","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L206-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.descFactF_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.descFactF_id","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L201-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_id","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L197-L199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prod_block_one_sub_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prod_block_one_sub_pow","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L189-L193","doc":"The content side at `f n = 1 − Qⁿ`: row `i`'s numerator block, cleared of division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prod_block_mul_descFactF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prod_block_mul_descFactF","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L171-L187","doc":"**A contiguous block of `f`-factors is a ratio of `descFactF`s**, division-free:\n\n`f(b)·f(b+1)⋯f(b+m−1) · descFactF f (b−1) = descFactF f (b+m−1)`.\n\nRow `i` of the level-`r` numerator is exactly such a block: its cells have content `j − i` for\n`j < μ_i`, so its factors are `f(r − i + j)`, a block starting at `b = r − i` of length `m = μ_i`.\nThe top index `b + m − 1 = μ_i + r − 1 − i` **is** the β-number `β_i`, which is why the\n`∏_i descFactF f β_i` produced here cancels against the one the hook side produces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.descFactF_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.descFactF_succ","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L162-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_mul_betaGapProdF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_mul_betaGapProdF","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L134-L154","doc":"**The per-row Frame–Robinson–Thrall identity, in any commutative monoid.**\n\nFor a weakly-decreasing tail `t` with every part `≤ a`,\n\n`rowHookProdF f a t · betaGapProdF f a t = descFactF f (a + |t|)`.\n\nAt `f = id` over `(ℕ, ×)` this is `SYTBeta.rowHookProd_mul_betaGapProd`; at `f n = 1 − Q^n` over a\nfield it is the q-analogue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_cons_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_cons_mul","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L71-L132","doc":"**The inductive step, in any commutative monoid.**\n\n`rowHookProdF f a (c :: r) · f(a + 1 − c) = rowHookProdF f (a+1) r`.\n\nSame reindexing as the `ℕ` proof: the prefix `j < c` matches the `(a+1)`-row factor at `j`, the tail\n`c ≤ j < a` matches it at `j+1`, and the β-gap `f(a + 1 − c)` supplies the missing middle factor at\n`j = c`.  Every `omega` below is about the `ℕ` **argument** of `f`, never about a value in `M` — which\nis exactly why the arithmetic of the original proof was incidental. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF_nil","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L68-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_cons","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_nil","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.descFactF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.descFactF","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L60-L61","doc":"`f(n)·f(n−1)⋯f(1)` — the `f`-analogue of `n!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The β-gap product pushed through `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProdF","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L51-L53","doc":"The row's hook lengths pushed through `f`: `∏_{j<a} f((a−j) + cnt t j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.list_range_map_prod'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.list_range_map_prod'","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid.lean#L41-L49","doc":"`SYTHookFormulaBeta.list_range_map_prod` is `ℕ`-specific; this is the same bridge in any\ncommutative monoid. ","signatureChunk":0}]}